WEBVTT

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:14.280
What?!

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.480
What the hell is that?

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.740
A dull blade?

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.420
The transfer student's done something weird again.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:21.120
Did he give up the fight?

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:23.120
I see.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:26.470
So that's why you didn't come to the fish market this morning.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:26.960
Huh?

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:31.170
You chose aging as a way to compensate for the difference in ingredient quality.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:35.760
I could tell what you used to age the fish just by looking at it.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:40.300
But that's not enough to reach the best of what the season has to offer.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:43.480
You won't know that for sure until you eat it.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.770
I'll cook enough for you guys to try too.

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:47.080
Yeah, right.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.650
The outcome's already clear.

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:50.860
Congratulations on finishing third.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:53.320
That's good enough to be rightfully proud.

00:00:55.060 --> 00:01:00.120
Honored guests, the time for the Autumn Selection Grand Finale to begin is almost here!

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:02.580
Please look up at the ceiling!

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.750
Wow!

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:10.960
The ceiling's splitting open!

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:12.710
Soon.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:16.340
This is Gatten Hall as it truly is.

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:20.760
The cooking time in the grand finale will span approximately two hours.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:23.670
This is the time it takes from the moment the moon appears in full,

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:25.020
traverses across the skies,

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:28.000
and becomes hidden once more.

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:30.510
Though it's the same every year,

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:32.060
it's still quite a spectacle.

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:36.440
<i>I fondly remember those days.</i>

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.700
<i>That night when I fought
 in the Autumn Selection grand finale....</i>

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:42.770
<i>All the chefs who have ever stood on this stage</i>

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:44.660
<i>have seen the same moon.</i>

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:48.830
<i>Don't lose to anyone else
 until you lose to me again next time!</i>

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:52.540
<i>I'm gonna gun for the top seat
 among Tohtsuki's first-years!</i>

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:53.670
Ready!

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:58.010
Let the cooking...

00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:00.980
begin!

00:02:01.970 --> 00:03:31.980
{OP}

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:26.620
Far beyond the image I have in my mind

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:33.090
The reality I'm building up is still far away

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.840
An endless journey

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:41.850
Let's hone each other's pride

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:44.350
Words aren't really important

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:46.850
So let's just say "yes" and leave it at that

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:53.820
We fight each other and hone our skills

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:58.700
Our encounters cause shockwaves

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.450
We're reckless challengers

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:06.450
Heading toward a world as yet unexplored

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:09.000
A swordsman should use his blade

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.830
To open the way to the future

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:17.550
This is my story and no one else's

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:37.190
None of the candidates have 
touched their Pacific saury.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:40.950
They'll start by prepping their other ingredients. Typical, I suppose.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:45.370
Working the fish more than necessary will negatively impact its freshness.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:48.950
They have to maintain the fish's freshness as much as possible.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.830
I'm being excited, yes.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:56.380
Watching young men... 
This is a sight for sore{was: hurting} eyes.{nice}

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:58.800
Oh, Mother, you're being rather inappropriate.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:01.590
And your vocabulary is skewed, as usual.

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:02.180
Alice!

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:04.140
Go back to your seat in the audience!

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:06.050
Erina, you should come over here too!

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:08.930
She can, can't she, Grandfather?

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:10.310
Yes. It doesn't matter.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:12.770
See, Erina?

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:15.650
What a fun family, Nakiri-kun.

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:17.270
Oh?

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:19.730
Yukihira seems to be handling his Pacific saury.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:22.820
Maybe the aging was a success?

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:25.410
Yeah. What kind of dish will he make with it?

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.780
Kurokiba Ryou. Hayama Akira.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:32.580
Can you win against those two monsters, Yukihira?

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:34.040
Ah!

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:37.670
So many different seafood ingredients on the young Kurokiba's prep surface!

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:41.010
I also see ripe tomatoes and olive oil.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:44.510
He probably intends to make acqua pazza.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:49.390
Acqua pazza is a regional dish from Southern Italy.

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:52.930
With fish as the main ingredient, many other ingredients are simmered into a stew.

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:55.140
It's a simple yet dynamic dish.

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:59.730
It's traditional to use olive oil,
 tomatoes, and shellfish.

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:02.610
It's also notable that the dish doesn't use much in the way of seasoning.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:07.030
Because of its simplicity, the quality of its ingredients comes to the fore.

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:09.580
It's a great dish to showcase his ability to judge his ingredients.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:13.540
But each and every ingredient is strong enough to be the main player.

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:16.120
Wouldn't blindly boiling them down together

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:19.210
actually eclipse the Pacific saury's strengths?

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:22.130
True, and the Pacific saury's in season too.

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:23.590
In season!

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:25.260
That's it.

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:27.760
Because it's in season, 
the Pacific saury won't be eclipsed.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.850
Rather, it has the potential to become a solid foundation for the entire dish.

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:35.560
He was able to select that dish precisely because
 he has confidence in his ability to judge ingredients.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:38.060
Above all, he's very calm.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:42.190
I don't sense any nerves or eagerness toward the match in him.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:43.480
Very impressive.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:45.360
Of course you wouldn't, Chef Doujima.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:49.530
Ryou-kun has faced me in cooking battles for a very long time now!

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:51.910
Brings back memories.

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:54.790
You were both so young. Very cute, you was.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:59.170
You knew him back when he was still in Scandinavia, Aunt Leonora.

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:01.040
Granny?!

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:02.550
How rude!

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:06.340
Showing off your youth! Selfish, Erina-chan!

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:07.430
That's not what I said!

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:10.140
"Aunt" and "Granny" are two different words!

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:13.310
So this is the boy, Alice?

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:14.770
Yes, Mother!

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:17.270
I want to make him my aide!

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:18.980
Let go. I'm prepping.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:21.480
Erina has a secretary now!

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.940
I want an aide around my own age too!

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:26.990
Well, we should ask your father.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:28.400
Don't act like I'm not even here!

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:31.120
I'm already the head chef of this restaurant!

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.160
I'm not gonna serve you—

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:35.200
I believe I told you to call me "miss."

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:35.790
Go home.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:37.910
Then let's do a cooking battle.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:39.040
Huh?

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:41.420
If you lose, become my loyal dog.

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:42.670
Woof, woof!

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:50.090
That little girl's dish was better.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:54.220
Come on. Say "woof" for me.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:58.640
Battle me one more time!

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:14.450
<i>Two years after our first match,</i>

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:16.240
<i>the moment's finally come!</i>

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:17.870
<i>I've won!</i>

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:20.330
His first victory!

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:26.380
We'll face off again tomorrow!

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:27.460
Okay, Ryou-kun?!

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:31.050
Fine... miss.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:34.390
I'll fight you any time.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:42.230
Then you'll be polite to me when I win next time?

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:43.190
No way!

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:51.780
Heat-resistant film?

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:54.160
What, it's not cling wrap?

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:59.080
It's capable of withstanding heat of greater than 200°C, and cold down to -40°C.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:02.420
Food can be wrapped in it and cooked.

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:07.130
<i>He's absorbed an arsenal of molecular gastronomy techniques from his battles with Alice.</i>

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:13.800
<i>His cooking now is not something he'd think up
 just from cooking in a port town pub.</i>

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:18.010
<i>This is indicative of their whole
 history working hard together.</i>

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:22.600
<i>Ryou-kun, don't lose, okay?</i>

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:26.270
<i>No need to remind me, miss.</i>

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:29.780
<i>This film is the key to my dish!</i>

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:31.240
Hayama!

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:33.990
I'll get you for sure this time!

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:39.580
The one who will stand at the top of this selection... will be me!

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:45.420
The moon's halfway across the sky!

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:48.380
Less than an hour left now.

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:49.250
Oh, look.

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:51.760
I'm done.

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:54.180
So first up is Kurokiba.

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:55.720
But...

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:57.510
Is that... really his dish?

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:59.310
In a hurry, huh?

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:02.310
Let's hope you didn't overlook anything in your dish.

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:05.560
Run your mouth while you still can.

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:08.860
My dish will crush your weapon.

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:14.240
What's Kurokiba trying to do with that flimsy film?

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:17.160
Something you're very familiar with, I bet.

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:20.950
Candidate Kurokiba will serve first!

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:25.870
<i>The moon serves to illuminate the candidate</i>

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:28.630
<i>who is advancing toward the judges like a stage light.</i>

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:33.800
<i>It's as though the light is purifying the chef and his dish!</i>

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:34.920
Wow!

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:38.220
Still simmering inside the pouch!

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:40.140
Very piping hot!

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:43.100
He's going to make the judges open the dish?

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:46.060
Now, have a taste!

00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:57.320
<i>Shrimp!</i>

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:58.280
<i>Mussels!</i>

00:09:58.280 --> 00:09:58.950
<i>Clams!</i>

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:00.450
<i>And Pacific saury!</i>

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:04.910
<i>I'm getting dragged into a torrent of different aromas!</i>

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:08.920
It's so good, my face is going slack!

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:10.630
Director!

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:14.510
He's usually so stern, yet he's grinning!

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:15.760
It's "the grin"!

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:17.840
Who knew we'd see the grin here?!

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:21.720
The ingredients are about the same as those in an acqua pazza,

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:25.930
but wrapping them in a heat-resistant film changes the dish's name.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:28.060
It's a cartoccio!

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:32.440
My dish is Autumn Pacific Saury Cartoccio!

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:38.950
<i>He served an umami detonator in the semi-finals.</i>

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:43.910
<i>He followed that up with an aroma detonator, I guess.</i>

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:45.370
<i>I see.</i>

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:47.960
Go on! Taste it!

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:55.250
So fresh! The Pacific saury's fat is meltingly sweet!

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:57.460
<i>The seafood ingredients are
 all extraordinarily fresh!</i>

00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:58.550
<i>There's more than enough umami!</i>

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:04.310
<i>Such power, sealing so much dynamic umami into this dish through sheer force...</i>

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:06.810
<i>This is Kurokiba Ryou's true worth!</i>

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:09.600
The Pacific saury may be in season,

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:13.150
but how could he craft such richness in flavor with so little seasoning?

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:15.730
Hm? What is this refreshing aroma?

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:17.900
It's not from seafood. It's...

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:19.780
It's from herbs.

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:21.280
That's right!

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:24.490
I added them to the packet when I wrapped the ingredient with the film.

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:26.990
I used this herb butter!

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:30.080
<i>After softening butter at room temperature,</i>

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:34.210
<i>he kneaded in finely chopped herbs, spices, and garlic.</i>

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:37.170
<i>The herb butter is complete after resting overnight in the fridge.</i>

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:41.340
It melted gradually from the heat in the oven,

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:43.590
and its richness and flavor

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:46.810
gradually seeped into the Pacific saury and other ingredients!

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:51.560
<i>It gave an incredible boost 
to the flavors and the fragrance!</i>

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:55.020
<i>It's a violence of flavor that is absolute!</i>

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:59.360
It seems we'll see my mother's "baring."

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:00.400
What?!

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:01.780
In somewhere this public?

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:02.610
Seriously?!

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:04.570
Th-That'd be really bad!

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:12.040
Huh?

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:13.710
What a wonderful Pacific saury dish.

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:15.880
First, it had immediate visual impact upon arriving at the table.

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:20.800
You have a firm grasp of the modern cooking trend that acknowledges the importance of a dish's aesthetics.

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:25.180
Given that the entire audience had leaned forward to look at the dish, your plan can be said to be a success.

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:30.270
Anchovies are often used in acqua pazza, but not in this dish, since herb butter was used.

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:32.480
When Mother eats something delicious, she sheds her broken 
Japanese and "bares" a fluent command of the language.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:31.480
That was wise.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:33.730
Adding both would have led to a clash of flavors.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:33.730
Right, I remember.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:37.230
The herb butter plays a critical role
 in establishing this dish.

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:36.440
Shedding broken Japanese?
 How's that work?!

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:40.360
The mellow butter serves to meld the flavors from each ingredient.

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:45.110
Its herbs impart a flavor that is strong, yet light and not overwhelming.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:50.660
<i>Flavors only made possible with Pacific saury in season, and no other fish!</i>

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:47.160
That further enhances the Pacific saury's aroma.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:51.330
The heat-resistant film and herb butter both serve to take full advantage of the Pacific saury's flavors.

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:54.120
<i>This is a culmination of his culinary techniques!</i>

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:54.120
His singular focus in doing so is what made this dish's flavors possible!

00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:57.790
<i>Body...</i>

00:12:57.790 --> 00:12:58.790
<i>...soul...</i>

00:12:59.290 --> 00:12:59.920
<i>...and ocean!</i>

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:03.670
<i>All as one!</i>

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:06.640
Kurokiba, that's amazing!

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:09.390
The director went bare-chested, too!

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:12.060
<i>Well?!</i>

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:16.400
<i>Sear my dish's power into your eyes, Hayama.</i>

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:19.520
Next, Candidate Hayama will serve his dish!

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:29.280
The hell, asshole?!

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:31.490
You think you can win against me
 with <i>that</i> kind of dish?!

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:34.000
Are you even being serious about this match?!

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:34.910
Forget it—

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:40.420
You don't know that aroma can recreate even the philosophy behind a dish.

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:41.750
<i>It can't be.</i>

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:43.260
<i>A carpaccio?!</i>

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:44.760
An antipasto?!

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:45.590
No way!

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:46.970
This is the grand finale!

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:48.840
How can he win with an antipasto dish?

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:53.560
<i>The antipasto is a dish intended to pique the diners' appetite at the start of a meal.</i>

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:56.310
<i>It is, by necessity, a lighter dish than others.</i>

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:57.810
<i>Why did he choose that?</i>

00:13:57.810 --> 00:13:59.100
<i>Hayama!</i>

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:02.570
<i>Your ability to judge ingredients is equal to mine.</i>

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:08.410
<i>I bet you tried to take advantage of the best Pacific saury's fresh flavor in the raw,</i>

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:11.700
<i>but there's no way your dish
 can contend with my cartoccio.</i>

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:14.370
<i>Not after it crushed the judges
 with its heavy umami and aroma!</i>

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:15.700
Well, let us taste—

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:17.330
Please wait a moment.

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:20.040
There's one last step.

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:23.090
He's searing the surface with a torch.

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:29.760
But that'd hardly be enough to counter the Kurokiba boy's aroma detonator.

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:37.020
Done.

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:42.770
My dish is Seared Pacific Saury Carpaccio!

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:45.860
Delicious.

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:46.530
Delicious!

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:48.110
It's delicious without even having a single taste!

00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:50.450
I can tell just how juicy it is!

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:52.370
It goes above and beyond what curing can do.

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:53.870
Wow!

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:55.660
The dish became completely different
 after the fish was seared.{pls try shorten}

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:59.830
Sizzle!

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:03.670
It's as though the dish is seducing everyone who is about to taste it!

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:04.380
Oh!

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.840
I can't wait... another... second!

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:15.180
The dressing consists of extra virgin olive oil, wine vinegar,

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:17.430
and Pacific saury innards!

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:21.350
The rich flavor of the innards floods the tongue and emphasizes the sweetness of the Pacific saury's fat!

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:23.810
I'm drowning in the overflowing aromas and flavors!

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:26.780
How many spices did you add to this dish?!

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:28.780
Nay!

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:31.740
He has only used allspice!

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:32.740
What?!

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:34.780
He only used one spice?

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:40.040
I thought Hayama's special weapon was to weave various spices into the best aroma possible.

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:41.670
<i>No.</i>

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:45.790
<i>His ability to manipulate fragrance is not just additive.</i>

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:49.720
He was able to highlight the seasonal flavor of Pacific saury with vivid clarity

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:52.050
by intentionally subtracting spices from the dish.

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:54.930
And yet, how did he manage
 such richness of fragrance?

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:58.350
It's on par with the aromatic force
 of Ryou-kun's cartoccio.

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:01.230
Yes, and it's not possible to achieve that through searing alone!

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:03.650
It's the kaeshi sauce.

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:06.570
I brushed it over the fish, right before serving.

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:07.860
The kaeshi?

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:09.610
Is that Tsubame Gaeshi?

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:10.780
Koujiro Sasaki?

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:12.990
I'm surprised you know that word.

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:13.910
But that's different.

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:18.160
Kaeshi is a seasoning made by a mixture of soy sauce with mirin, sake,

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:19.750
and other ingredients.

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:23.540
You can make soba dipping sauce by diluting kaeshi with stock.

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:27.420
It's considered an all-purpose seasoning for most Japanese dishes.

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:28.880
No wonder.

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:33.510
Fish is hard to sear, even with
 high heat from the torch.

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:37.470
Kaeshi contains sugar, which makes the fish much easier to sear.

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:39.350
So he prevented the loss of flavor

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:43.440
that would have resulted from a more prolonged exposure to heat.

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:46.810
The surface fat of the fish
 and the sugars in the kaeshi

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:49.070
sizzle and bubble from the heat.

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:52.190
In other words, I managed to demonstrate two theoretically opposing principles—

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:56.200
the subtraction of aroma and its emphasis—
in unison with this single dish.

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:58.740
<i>Kurokiba Ryou and Hayama Akira.</i>

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:02.040
<i>They both evolved because of their previous match.</i>

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:06.330
<i>Kurokiba Ryou wields a massive sword.</i>

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:11.760
<i>He further improved the explosive, appetizing power of his dish at the finals.</i>

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:15.220
<i>In contrast, the duck dish that Hayama Akira served at the semi-finals</i>

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:17.340
<i>was a brilliant feast of spices.</i>

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:20.930
<i>It was like a finely crafted, ornate sword.</i>

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:24.890
<i>But look at Hayama tonight.</i>

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:27.730
<i>Refinement through differentiation and selection</i>

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:31.730
<i>has produced a blade that is as sharp and fine as a well-honed rapier!</i>

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:47.000
What did you call me before?
 A one-trick pony with spices?

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:51.630
This is what it means to have 
absolute mastery over aroma.

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:56.840
<i>So this is the master of fragrance,
 Hayama Akira's, true worth!</i>

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:59.010
<i>This Pacific saury is such a pure force!</i>

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:00.800
<i>It unleashes its flavor with no pretense!</i>

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:04.810
<i>A well-aimed arrow is true!</i>

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:06.020
<i>Bravo!</i>

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:10.980
The director's gone bare-chested again!

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:11.900
Oh!

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:13.440
The moon's starting to set!

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:15.820
Hurry, Souma-kun!

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:18.700
Yukihira, you're running out of time!

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:29.830
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:31.670
This will be the finish!

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:39.300
This is irresistible to anyone
 who eats rice on a daily basis.

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:41.090
It's enough to make you smile
 purely from reflex...

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:43.890
from the sight of it and the destructive aroma!

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:46.220
It's Salted Rice Bran Pacific Saury Rice.

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:47.020
Salted rice bran?!

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:47.890
Pickled with salted rice bran?!

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:49.440
So he didn't give up.

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:51.400
It looks delicious!

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:56.070
Well, I was thinking {it would be }the worst case scenario when I saw that dull-looking Pacific saury.

00:18:56.070 --> 00:19:00.910
Yeah, I guess it looked dull because it'd been pickled in salted rice bran.

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:05.540
I can't bear the piping hot fragrance!

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:06.910
Yes, yes.

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:08.330
I'll serve you right away.

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:09.870
Please wait just a moment.

00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:11.500
Oh, Yukihira-kun!

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:13.750
What a tease! Hurry!

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:17.960
<i>The other two were also creative about heightening our expectations,</i>

00:19:17.960 --> 00:19:20.760
<i>but Yukihira Souma is not taking a back seat to them!</i>

00:19:20.760 --> 00:19:24.300
<i>He knows how to make his guests eager for his dish!</i>

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:25.470
Here it comes!

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:27.020
Finally!

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:29.020
Now, let's taste!

00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:41.530
The happiness of Pacific saury brought by autumn
 is spreading throughout my body!

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:44.490
What gentle flavor!

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:46.160
He grilled the fish on a
 clay cooking stove first—

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:48.250
He grilled it first,
 then cooked it with the rice!

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:53.080
Such meticulous prep work allowed this much of the Pacific saury's aroma to transfer to the rice!

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:54.840
And the Pacific saury itself is marvelous too!

00:19:54.840 --> 00:20:00.170
With every bite, the deep umami and fragrant aroma bursts forth from the saltiness into your mouth!

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:02.800
This is on par with the Pacific saury in the other two's dishes!

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:06.300
Is this deep flavor due to the salted rice bran?!

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:11.730
Indeed. It's a traditional favorite from Hokkaido.

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:15.900
The salted rice bran draws out an ingredient's umami,
 removes any bad smells, and improves the nutritional value.

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:20.360
Some insist that it is the best
 preparation for Pacific saury.

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:24.950
Still, I'm impressed you managed to improve the flavor to this degree, Yukihira.

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:27.660
I took a big risk. It was a race against time!

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:32.370
I bought as many high-quality Pacific saury from the fish market as I could

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:34.080
and kept testing aging methods.

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:38.340
Of course, I tried and improved other aging methods than salted rice bran too.

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:42.300
It was hard to make something that could compete with top-quality Pacific saury in season,

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:46.720
but I finally found one that was satisfactory right before the match.

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:48.640
That was this fish, aged using salted rice bran!

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:52.520
<i>Hints from Fumio-san's words, the salted rice bran pickles at the dorm,</i>

00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:55.150
<i>all the tips and tricks about aging
 I learned from my friends...</i>

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:58.690
<i>All of it contributed to my inspiration!</i>

00:20:58.690 --> 00:21:01.740
He discovered that aging method on his own?!

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:03.320
Though we thought it
 was a worthless blade,

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:08.370
it has shown itself to be a fine sword!

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:12.120
Just like a swordsmith who forges
 steel into a fine blade,

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:17.080
he has created that sword of autumn on his own!

00:21:25.180 --> 00:22:51.930
{ED}

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:51.080
An intensely burning desire was born

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:56.920
But not in me, in someone else

00:21:56.920 --> 00:22:01.720
Where's the me who believed that

00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:06.850
All one needs is to have hopes and dreams

00:22:06.850 --> 00:22:12.100
Wrapped around something long, my compass was lost

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:17.860
On the border of life and death, snow drops bloom

00:22:17.860 --> 00:22:23.200
If by some mistake they get smashed

00:22:23.200 --> 00:22:28.370
At least put flowers on the empty husk

00:22:28.370 --> 00:22:34.040
Is that the way things are? Yes, it is

00:22:34.040 --> 00:22:39.090
You can call it resignation if you want

00:22:39.090 --> 00:22:45.010
But that's not me, that's not me

00:22:45.010 --> 00:22:49.640
There's no value in something just anyone could make

00:22:54.260 --> 00:22:56.020
Souma-kun's amazing!

00:22:56.020 --> 00:22:57.350
Yeah! No complaints here!

00:22:57.350 --> 00:22:59.140
I bet he'll get high marks for that!

00:22:59.140 --> 00:22:59.980
Oh!

00:22:59.980 --> 00:23:02.190
The director hasn't gone bare-chested!

00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:02.810
H-Hey.

00:23:02.810 --> 00:23:03.230
Yeah.

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:03.650
Right.

00:23:04.400 --> 00:23:07.860
Chef Doujima and Ms. Leonora have also already rested their chopsticks!

00:23:07.860 --> 00:23:08.780
That means...

00:23:08.780 --> 00:23:10.200
<i>Hm...</i>

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:14.530
<i>Did the Yukihira boy spend too much time trying to close the ingredient quality gap?</i>

00:23:14.910 --> 00:23:17.830
<i>In terms of creativity, his dish
 is not on par with those two!</i>

00:23:18.370 --> 00:23:20.460
Of course he couldn't hope to compete with them.

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:21.460
Yeah.

00:23:21.830 --> 00:23:23.920
Like I thought, the match will be between...

00:23:23.920 --> 00:23:25.670
Kurokiba and Hayama!

00:23:25.670 --> 00:23:27.920
I'd like you to have seconds too.

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:30.430
Does no one want more?

00:23:31.550 --> 00:23:33.470
It's the end of the line.

00:23:33.890 --> 00:23:34.930
Souma-kun!

00:23:40.390 --> 00:23:42.980
With this, we conclude the evaluation—

00:23:42.980 --> 00:23:45.480
If it means you'd have seconds,

00:23:45.480 --> 00:23:48.360
I'd like you to pour this over the rice and dig in.

00:23:48.360 --> 00:23:49.360
Hm!

00:23:52.360 --> 00:23:54.990
My Pacific saury dish...

00:23:55.660 --> 00:23:57.490
is not yet complete.

00:23:58.700 --> 00:24:03.920
I'll show you this blade's real edge!

00:24:07.380 --> 00:24:10.920
Next time, "A New Genius."
